{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/the-earthbane-cycle/at-the-gates/1533780-sell-me-on-at-the-gates","id":1533780,"title":"Sell me on At the Gates","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Earthbane Cycle","At the Gates"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-07T19:01:15-07:00","id":1533780,"title":"Sell me on At the Gates","content":"So we are few weeks till the crowdfunding of <b>At the Gates</b> game. ( <b>AtG</b> for short from now. ) We got some previews <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/earthbane/at-the-gates/\" target=\"_blank\">blog posts about it</a> and some tease here and there on Pathcasts. So let's see if you can sell me this game...<br /> <br /> (Correct me if I'm wrong) <b>At the Gates</b> is jRPG-like setting. We talk here about things like <b>Final Fantasy </b>(<b> FF </b>for short ) , and more like 8 and 9, than 7 - those first two were much more traditional fantasy and 7 was much more urban fantasy. So how does this compare to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fabula_Ultima\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Fabula Ultima</b></a>, other jRPG great system from last year? ( We literally have now in Poland crowdfunding for translation <b>Fabula</b>, right now. )<br /> <br /> In <b>AtG</b> we have world of Gaia, where 'world is returning from magical apocalypse' ( World Below? ), briming with magic. Even peasants have spells right now. There is something called <b>the Void</b> ( analog to <b>MtAw</b> or <b>Exalted</b> Abyss? ), we have Deamons ( I assume they are like <b>FF</b> Summons ), we have <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/at-the-gates-creatures-of-gaia/\" target=\"_blank\">Elemental Dragons and Elemental beings</a>. We also have Bat and Bear-People in previews.<br /> <br /> Something I missed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-14-2024, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-11T09:30:52-07:00","id":1534026,"title":"","content":"Is it me - or <b>At The Gates</b> Daemons (antagonists ) are VERY like <b>CoD</b> Spirits, only much more materialized! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/at-the-gates-daemons/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/at-the-gates-daemons/\" target=\"_blank\"> [At the Gates] Daemons &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/at-the-gates-daemons/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://theonyxpath.com/at-the-gates-daemons/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-11T09:43:04-07:00","id":1534029,"title":"","content":"Danielle in <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/argh-my-eyes-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">this week Monday Meeting Notes</a> is writing on design concepts of AtG and how she implemented them:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monday Meeting Notes</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>At the Gates</b><br /> <br /> Since the ashcan came out, and we\u2019re getting ready to crowdfund this hopefully soon, I wanted to chat a little bit about what <b>At the Gates</b> is, what it isn\u2019t, and why it exists.When I first started working on Storypath, before I ever did the update, I thought the system would work really well for a high-fantasy spell-slinging game. I spent some time coming up with an idea for what kind of fantasy game <i>I\u2019d</i> like to see and play, and it involved people who are diverse, but diversity isn\u2019t gamified. A setting that had a variety of play styles for fantasy, but focused on being heroic. A game that had clear goals, hooks, and made it clear from the beginning what it is you\u2019re supposed to be doing in it. So, I set to work creating this kind of setting. I am a huge fan of political intrigue, hard choices, moral ambiguity, and exploring the other through a lense of curiosity and compassion. So, of course, I put all that into my setting. As I was writing things up, I realized how much games like <i>Final Fantasy 9, Chrono Trigger, The Secret of Mana,</i> and others were influencing what I was writing. The further I got into the concept, the more I realized I had pretty much written the setting of a JRPG that didn\u2019t exist. When I pitched the game to Rich (back in 2019, in the before-times) it wasn\u2019t originally conceptually a jrpg, but he suggested that we just lean into it. So I did.<br /> I tweaked a few things here and there, but honestly, it was already there. Then when we started working on SP Ultra, I knew that this game was going to be very suited to its style. I was able to add in the concept of magical attacks, teamwork stunts that you can purchase with your bond Enhancement, and a slew of other really fun things that harken to playing a JRPG. If you\u2019re knowledgeable about those games, you\u2019ll see little bits here and there that remind you of many different games. If you aren\u2019t familiar with JRPGs at all, that\u2019s okay. I crafted the world to be rich and full of fun concepts that anyone can enjoy, you aren\u2019t missing anything by not noticing the inspirations, because we didn\u2019t decide to make the game referential.<br /> <br /> If you like fantasy games where the heroes are competent, it encourages you to explore, make hard choices, engage in political issues, fight against evil, and be big heroes, then I think you\u2019ll enjoy <b>At the Gates. </b><br /> <br /> Danielle</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-12T08:46:00-07:00","id":1534096,"title":"","content":"I've been looking for a long time for a game that scratches my itch for a JRPG-inspired game like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anima_(role-playing_game)\" target=\"_blank\">Anima</a>, (Awesome setting, terrible system). So far the only one who even comes close is Fabula Ultima, but it doesn't really reach the level of epicness I'm looking for, probably because it doesn't have a default setting. I'm finding the premise of At the Gates interesting, but the demo hasn't shown me yet enough to make a strong impression on me. I think we need to wait for the Kickstarter and have more info before we can give a good argument in favor, or against, it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-13T23:14:40-07:00","id":1534182,"title":"","content":"<b>Vision of Mana 2024</b> commercial, returning to previous games in series - maybe adds a bit ideas for At the Gates. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( There are English subtitles on YT. ) <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7WXSZWbYHs8\" data-code=\"7WXSZWbYHs8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/7WXSZWbYHs8/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T07:30:02-07:00","id":1534248,"title":"","content":"In latest Pathcast, Danielle is talking about <b>Big Picture take on AtG</b> - from around 47:35 of episode! \ud83d\ude2e<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.podbean.com/ea/pb-g8ihb-15dc794\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.podbean.com/ea/pb-g8ihb-15dc794</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-02T08:58:57-07:00","id":1535074,"title":"","content":"Danielle much more on <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/almost-at-the-gates-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>At the Gates</b> mechanics in contrast to <b>Chrono Trigger</b></a>...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monday Meeting Notes</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The third and most important reason is that a lot of the cool powers and abilities that you can do in <b>Chrono Trigger</b> gave inspiration to what you can do in <b>At the Gates.</b> I talk about it during the playthrough, but the fact that every character has an elemental affinity and special techniques they can learn on their own, and then combination techniques that they can perform with others. In <b>At the Gates</b> all characters have a set of Arts (special techniques) and Pillars of magic they can cast, and they can choose to utilize bond Enhancement to purchase special Tricks that act as combo Tricks.<br /> <br /> I have also been answering some FAQ style questions that some people asked while I\u2019m playing. A lot of it is mechanical considerations, reasons for making some of the choices I did, and other behind the scenes things that you won\u2019t get just from reading the manuscript.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d love it if you join me on Tuesday at 5pm EST to play through Chrono Trigger and talk about At the Gates. This week I\u2019ll be answering more questions, and next week I\u2019ll be celebrating the Backerkit launch! I\u2019ll also answer any questions you put into chat as I play, so this is a great opportunity to hit me with burning questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-12T22:11:05-07:00","id":1535501,"title":"","content":"Reading now <b>At the Gates Preview 1</b> - It me, or setting for<b> AtG</b> is just much less eastern <b>Exalted</b>, with Charms changes to martial techniques of Arts and Summoning of Daemons? <b>What is really unique for this game, compared even to others of Onyx Path?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-13T06:25:38-07:00","id":1535510,"title":"","content":"While my knowledge of Exalted is fairly minimal, I don\u2019t see the connection other than vaguely saying both properties are partially inspired by Eastern media properties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-13T23:27:50-07:00","id":1535545,"title":"","content":"At <b><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/episode/1fTxb8gqMIlxZUDeHO4iz2?si=XXVngkQDRmm-RombTqTdnQ&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=396a7b3dee774386\" target=\"_blank\">Character Creation for <i>At the Gates</i> podcast</a></b> Danielle points that:<ul><li><b>Daemons</b> are thinly vailed allegory for Atomic Weapons! \ud83d\ude32</li> <li>Most people in the setting have 'living magic's inside them - and you have many aesthetic special features added for free, like your skin is rock, you got bunny ears or crystals are coming from your skin. \ud83d\ude32 ( No mechanical difference, as I understood podcast. )</li> <li>In the settting there is a big <b>Magical Steampunk</b> and science elements also! ( Quote from preview <i>-'When the people of Everend speak of technology, thus, they mean steam harnessed by spirits, intricate brass coils catching the essence of the elements, and crystal cogs powered by magic.'</i>)</li> <li>Arts - <b>Technique skills</b>: Many require Momentum - <i><b>Desperation Ability</b></i> ( your <i>Final Fantasy</i>-like Limit Breaks) - That needs O ( ZERO ) Momentum in the pool! R<i><b>eadiness Abilities</b></i> - that needs 'AT Least this' number of Momentum.</li> <li><b>Magic</b> - Main Four <i>Pillars</i> ( Schools of Magic ) are - <b>Anima</b> is the magic of the body and Soul, Cognition is the magic of the mind and others, <b>Elementalism</b> is the magic of the land and elements, and <b>Transmutation</b> is the magic of change and manipulating magic itself.</li> <li>One of 3 blocks of Pillar is you <b>Keystone</b> - 3 different cooldowns types on them: <b>Instinct</b> cast every single <i><b>round</b></i>, <b>Elevated</b> - cast only once a <b><i>scene</i></b>, and <b>Iconic </b>- cast once a <b><i>session</i></b>. You can refresh Elevated and Iconic by spending <i><b>Energy</b></i>. For <b>Keystone</b>, you can refresh Iconic and Elevated refresh them for free once per session.( Choose Keystone by looking what you want to cast twice per session. )</li> </ul><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/episode/1fTxb8gqMIlxZUDeHO4iz2?si=XXVngkQDRmm-RombTqTdnQ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/episode/1fTxb8gqMIlxZUDeHO4iz2?si=XXVngkQDRmm-RombTqTdnQ\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/episode/1fTxb8gqMIlxZUDeHO4iz2?si=XXVngkQDRmm-RombTqTdnQ\" target=\"_blank\"> https://open.spotify.com/episode/1fTxb8gqMIlxZUDeHO4iz2?si=XXVngkQDRmm-RombTqTdnQ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-14-2024, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T04:17:06-07:00","id":1535551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/the-earthbane-cycle/at-the-gates/1533780-sell-me-on-at-the-gates?p=1535501#post1535501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading now <b>At the Gates Preview 1</b> - It me, or setting for<b> AtG</b> is just much less eastern <b>Exalted</b>, with Charms changes to martial techniques of Arts and Summoning of Daemons? <b>What is really unique for this game, compared even to others of Onyx Path?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's still too early to tell without having all the chapters to provide more context. That said, the uniqueness of this setting, at least for me, is based on the dish's flavor and not the dish itself. Let me elaborate. It's a fantasy RPG, we have a couple of them in Onyx Path and hundreds of them from other companies and indie developers, true, but this time Ony Path is going for a specific type that they have never tried before: JRPGs. With that objective in mind, the question is: Have they captured the &quot;flavor&quot;? Does it &quot;feel&quot; like a JRPG? My answer is yes, I think they have done a good job so far, reading the first two chapters has transported me to my ps1 and ps2 eras of playing JRPGS. However, I also admit it's a matter of personal preference and subjective experience, it's all about what you're looking for.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Most people in the setting have 'living magic's inside them - and you have many aesthetic special features added for free, like your skin is rock, you got bunny ears or crystals are coming from your skin. \ud83d\ude32 ( No mechanical difference, as I understood podcast. )&quot;</b><br /> <br /> Pardon me, maybe I'm remembering it wrong but listening to the podcast my understanding was that you had an option during character creation to make those features relevant if you wanted it. I think it was divided into two levels, with the first giving you something like sharper senses and the second giving you something more radical like wings or breathing underwater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 05-15-2024, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T09:41:57-07:00","id":1535646,"title":"","content":"On <b>Backerkit</b> page there is short story in the world of <b>At the Gates</b> - <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.backerkit.com/c/projects/onyx-path/at-the-gates/updates/6610?ref=bk-noti-project-update-6610\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.backerkit.com/c/projects...ct-update-6610</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T06:24:33-07:00","id":1536054,"title":"","content":"Okay, Rules Chapter bought my heart with classical jRPG <b>Fishing Minigame</b>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img width=\"638\" height=\"330\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/j2T4YLH.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/j2T4YLH.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/j2T4YLH.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-21-2024, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}